---
description: ViewerOne cloud-agent working style
alwaysApply: true
---

- Do not ask the user to reconfigure MIDI, Cubase, loopMIDI, or hardware.
- Desktop/taskbar launch errors must be visible (message box or console). Never swallow shortcut failures with On Error Resume Next.
- Capturing VBScript `WScript.Shell.Run` requires parentheses: `exitCode = sh.Run(command, 0, True)`.
- If a local shortcut is already broken, it cannot update itself from GitHub. Ship `ViewerOne-Fix.cmd` and say so plainly.
